# Global Project Rules

## Purpose
Keep all generated work aligned with the architecture, stack, and scaffold specs as the single source of truth.

## Scope
All files, all agents, and all generated code in this repository.

## Hard Constraints
- MUST follow `specs/01-architecture.md`, `specs/02-stack.md`, and `specs/03-scaffold.md`.
- MUST NOT introduce new frameworks, libraries, folders, or conventions without updating the specs first.
- MUST keep changes deterministic, minimal, and aligned to the existing scaffold.
- MUST prefer enforceable rules over prose-only guidance.

## Best Practices
- SHOULD reuse existing modules, tokens, and shared utilities before creating new ones.

## Enforceability
- Lint: repository-wide import, style, and boundary rules.
- CI: spec drift checks and type checks.
- Review: reject any code that conflicts with the approved specs.

## Examples
### ✅ Valid
```ts
import { Button } from '@charts-gen/ui';
```

### ❌ Invalid
```ts
import { Button } from '../../packages/design-system/components/Button';
```
